From: ksre-ps5
Subject: configure: accept a FreeBSD --host when cross compiling

CPython 3.12's configure refuses cross builds for any host it does not list
(Linux, Cygwin, VxWorks, Emscripten, WASI). The PS5 payload target is
FreeBSD-derived (clang x86_64-sie-ps5 defines __FreeBSD__, FreeBSD headers),
so the port configures with --host=x86_64-unknown-freebsd. This adds that host
to the two case statements: ac_sys_system=FreeBSD (selects configure's existing
FreeBSD branches) and _PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM=freebsd-x86_64. ac_sys_release
stays empty, so MACHDEP and sys.platform are "freebsd".

The generated configure is patched the same way, so autoreconf is not needed.

SPDX-License-Identifier: PSF-2.0
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -559,6 +559,9 @@
 	*-*-wasi)
 	    ac_sys_system=WASI
 	    ;;
+	*-*-freebsd*)
+		ac_sys_system=FreeBSD
+		;;
 	*)
 		# for now, limit cross builds to known configurations
 		MACHDEP="unknown"
@@ -619,6 +622,9 @@
 	wasm32-*-* | wasm64-*-*)
 		_host_cpu=$host_cpu
 		;;
+	*-*-freebsd*)
+		_host_cpu=$host_cpu
+		;;
 	*)
 		# for now, limit cross builds to known configurations
 		MACHDEP="unknown"
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -4279,6 +4279,9 @@
 	*-*-wasi)
 	    ac_sys_system=WASI
 	    ;;
+	*-*-freebsd*)
+		ac_sys_system=FreeBSD
+		;;
 	*)
 		# for now, limit cross builds to known configurations
 		MACHDEP="unknown"
@@ -4341,6 +4344,9 @@
 	wasm32-*-* | wasm64-*-*)
 		_host_cpu=$host_cpu
 		;;
+	*-*-freebsd*)
+		_host_cpu=$host_cpu
+		;;
 	*)
 		# for now, limit cross builds to known configurations
